        <definition>std::optional&lt; VGRemap &gt; AGRemapCore::ModAssets&lt; std::string, VGRemap, std::equal_to&lt;std::string&gt; &gt;::get</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::vector&lt; std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; &gt; &amp;nonVersionVals, const std::vector&lt; std::optional&lt; Version &gt; &gt; &amp;versionVals, bool errorOnNotFound=true) const</argsstring>
        <name>get</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::ModAssets&lt; std::string, VGRemap &gt;::get</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>nonVersionVals</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; std::optional&lt; <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_version" kindref="compound">Version</ref> &gt; &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>versionVals</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>errorOnNotFound</declname>
          <defval>true</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Retrieves the corresponding asset. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nonVersionVals</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
One entry per non-version column, in their relative index order (version columns
skipped) -- ``std::nullopt`` at a position means &quot;match any value there&quot;. Must have
exactly #getNonVersionColumnCount elements
</verbatim> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>versionVals</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
One entry per version column, in their relative index order -- ``std::nullopt`` at a
position means &quot;use the latest available value for this column, among rows still
matching everything resolved so far&quot;. Must have exactly #getVersionColumnCount
elements :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Version columns are resolved **sequentially, in index order** -- each one&apos;s
floor-match (largest available value :math:`\leq` the target; the smallest available
value if none qualifies) narrows the candidate set before the next version column is
resolved against it
</verbatim> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>errorOnNotFound</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to throw if no matching asset is found</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If &apos;nonVersionVals&apos;/&apos;versionVals&apos; don&apos;t have exactly <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_assets_1a07131484934a4fedeb84a6c0bd4a1f5b" kindref="member">getNonVersionColumnCount</ref>/<ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_assets_1a45436dbb5bfc86d39fcd079eddcbcadf" kindref="member">getVersionColumnCount</ref> elements respectively </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::out_of_range</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If no matching asset is found and &apos;errorOnNotFound&apos; is <computeroutput>true</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The found asset, or <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> if none is found and &apos;errorOnNotFound&apos; is <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
